U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>63095388</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7336786-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7336786</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1120990A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TEMCO JAPAN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEMCO JAPAN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A transmitter/receiver for telephones and radio devices which is small, lightweight, and comfortably wearable. The user can hear the party without difficulty even in noisy surroundings, can talk so low in public that people around the user do not feel offensive and can talk while even listening to music through a headset. The transmitter/receiver can be also used as a personal ornament. The transmitter/receiver comprises a bone-conduction speaker (2), a microphone (3), and a drive circuit case (4), and is connectable to a telephone set or a radio device. The bone-conduction speaker (2) can be set at an arbitrarily place on the face of the user when the microphone (3) is placed near the mouth of the user.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un émetteur-récepteur pour téléphones et dispositifs radio qui est petit, léger et confortable à porter. L'utilisateur peut entendre son interlocuteur sans difficulté même dans des environnements bruyants, parler en public d'une voix si faible que les gens qui l'entourent ne se sentent pas agressés, et peut même parler en écoutant de la musique par un casque. L'émetteur-récepteur peut également être utilisé comme ornement personnel. L'émetteur-récepteur comporte un haut-parleur (2) à conduction osseuse, un microphone (3) et un boîtier (4) de circuit d'excitation, et peut être branché sur un combiné de téléphone ou sur un dispositif radio. L'utilisateur peut fixer le haut-parleur (2) à conduction osseuse sur son visage à un endroit choisi arbitrairement lorsqu'il place le microphone (3) à côté de sa bouche.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>